<article class="env-lemma" id="06RN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06RN">Lemma <span data-tag="06RN">10.31.10</span>.</a> Any surjective endomorphism of a Noetherian ring is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $f : R \to R$ were such an endomorphism but not injective, then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(f) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(f \circ f) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(f \circ f \circ f) \subset \ldots  \]
</div>
    <p>
       would be a strictly increasing chain of ideals. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>